<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37479" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecursor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>one who runs before.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A forerunner</i>, <i>precursor</i>,
			of a servant, <i><span class="en">Plin. Pan. 76</span></i>
			<i>fin.; one who precedes on the same path</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Lact. 6, 7, 3</span></i>.— 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Esp.,</span>”
				<i>the forerunner of Christ</i>, <i>John the
					Baptist</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Aug. Tract. in Johan. 4, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">4,
			8</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flos praecursor indolis bonae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Nazar. Pan. Const. 3 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b> In
			milit. lang., <i>an advanced guard</i>, <i>vanguard</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 26, 17
					<i>fin.</i></span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a scout</i>, <i>spy</i> (cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">emissarius, speculator),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. Verr. 2, 5, 41, § 108</span></i>
			. 
			</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
